## Summary

Delivered a production-grade, native SwiftUI parity of `components/feedback/ReloadPrompt.tsx` as a new **10-file shared surface** at `apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/ReloadPrompt.*`, following the just-merged AIUsageCard decomposition pattern:

- **`ReloadPrompt.swift`** – surface view, phase switch, `role="alert"`/`aria-live` → VoiceOver announcement, lifecycle.
- **`.Model.swift`** – i18n facade (P1/S10), telemetry seam (P1/S11 `view.opened`), state-holder seam (P1/S8) + in-memory source, `@Observable` model with countdown logic.
- **`.Adapter.swift` / `.Projection.swift`** – pure web-parity logic (countdown reducer, module constants, phase resolution).
- **`.Timing.swift`** – injectable countdown ticker (structured-concurrency `Timer` + manual test driver).
- **`.Chrome.swift` / `.Views.swift`** – freshness chip, re-check button, connectivity banner, loading skeleton, error+retry, the update-available countdown banner, and the up-to-date empty body.
- **`.Previews.swift` / `.Tests.swift` / `.strings`** – per-state previews, 22 XCTest cases, full i18n catalog.

**Parity covered:** all 4 web i18n keys (`pwa.newVersion/reloadingIn/later/reloadNow`), 3s auto-reload countdown, Later/Reload Now, plus the mandated `checking/upToDate/error/stale/offline` states (no hidden surfaces), null-safety, a11y labels, and telemetry.

**Verification (every runnable check green):** `swiftc -typecheck` of the logic core, the **full surface UI against the real design tokens/components**, and the test logic — all under Swift 6 strict concurrency; `swiftc -parse` on all files; `swiftformat --lint` (0); `swiftlint --strict` (**0 surface violations**); `check-placeholders` (0); `xcodegen generate` (wiring valid, 60 refs in the project).

**Necessary wiring** (documented, not silent): registered `TeslaSync/shared-surfaces` in `project.yml` (iOS+macOS) and `.swiftlint.yml` — without it the new directory is dead code.

